        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: route direct outbound polls through channel adapters",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where core poll sends for direct channel plugins still went through the message gateway path, so agent/channel poll fallback could fail or misroute even when the selected channel exposed `outbound.sendPoll` directly.\n\nAI-assisted: yes.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`sendPoll` now follows the same delivery-mode split as message sends: direct and hybrid outbound adapters use the plugin `sendPoll` fallback with existing target resolution, while gateway-mode adapters keep using the gateway poll RPC. The shared poll path also preserves the existing duration/anonymity support gates, and CLI formatting now reports direct core polls as direct deliveries instead of gateway deliveries.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAgents and CLI message actions can send polls through direct-capable channel plugins without requiring gateway poll routing, while unsupported poll options still fail clearly instead of being silently ignored.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/commands/message-format.test.ts src/infra/outbound/format.test.ts src/infra/outbound/message.channels.test.ts src/infra/outbound/outbound-send-service.test.ts src/infra/outbound/message-action-runner.poll.test.ts`\n- `pnpm tsgo:test:src`\n- `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD`\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode branch --base upstream/main` -> clean, no accepted/actionable findings\n",
